    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Derek Schmidt has been a state senator in Kansas Attorney General and quite nearly governor in Topeka, but his next job will take him to Washington, D.C. Congressman Elect Schmidt is the state's newest addition to the U.S. House and will represent the second district for the next two years starting in January. He won a competitive primary and coasted through the November general election by emphasizing well-known Republican talking points, border security and inflation. He also praised President-elect Donald Trump and expressed a philosophy of government that was labeled defending our way alive and getting government out of our way. Mr. Former Senator, Attorney General, welcome back to the Kansas Reflector Podcast.",
