        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener will be a member of Congress at some point next month.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The listener is currently considering or preparing to run for Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the listener's election to Congress is certain or highly likely.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Membership in Congress is something that can be achieved through personal effort and timing.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener understands the reference to 'this time next month' as referring to their future role in Congress.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Answer"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 92921,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92921.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, it's very real, not to state the obvious, but we're under three weeks now until swearing in, which will be January 3rd. We've been in the process of doing all those things great and small that you have to do to prepare, boning up on issues, working on relationships with other new members, working on relationships with some of the leadership, making sure we stay connected with Kansas, getting staff in place, getting office in place, all those sort of housekeeping things as well. that have to do so that we can start on January 3rd and really be effective. I think, you know, we're going to have a continued Republican majority in the House slimmer a bit than it was, but a continued Republican majority, a new Republican majority in the Senate, and obviously a Republican president. There's not a lot of time to waste. There are going to be windows of opportunity, I hope, I believe, to, you know, make progress on some of these things we've all been talking about, but that won't last forever. So we have to be ready to start quickly, and I hope we will.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
