    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "think so. And I think we don't have to solve every problem, but we have to make progress on many of the things that we've talked about. We have to show folks that they've entrusted us with the ability to represent them to lead, and that trust is well placed in terms of getting some stuff done. There's a set of polling data. It's public. I was reading a news article on it this morning. I thought it was really interesting. It's some exit polling data that suggested that one of the real drivers in the election this year, and especially the presidential, was a large desire just to get something done. It wasn't so much that folks want this or that. It's that they want something to happen, to show motion, which they then can judge as to whether it's progress or not. That's consistent with, I think, a lot of the coffee shop talk around the second district.",
