    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "I'm very happy that just got notified yesterday that I got both of those. So those will be my two committee assignments. I think armed services is very important for the district as well as obviously for the country. I mean, we face a time when, you know, America's positioning around the world is a bit challenging, a bit in flux. And in the second congressional district, we obviously have a very large military presence. So we have two of the Army's divisions headquartered here with the 35th Infantry at Fort Leavenworth and the first infantry at Fort Riley. We have the air refueling wing at Forbes. So, you know, a big gas station, as some say, or a tanker base. We have the headquarters of the Kansas Guard, lots of local guard units around the district. And as well as a large veterans and military support presence. And so, you know, I think that's an area I can help fill a gap that would be very good for the state and for the second district in particular. And then Judiciary. Probably not terribly surprising. I'll be the only former state attorney general serving in the house next year. And, you know, I like to think that'll help me bring a perspective that might be helpful on the committee. At least a majority of folks who decided these things seem to agree. So I'll look forward to it.",
