    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "I don't think we're there at this point. I think we let Tom Holman, who's going to be the so-called czar on the border and immigration, as well as the others who are in a position, formal positions to actually run the apparatus of the federal government that deals with all of these, this basket of issues, Let them take office let them move to implement the president's priorities, and then we'll see where we are I don't think we need to sort of jump to but by the way We haven't we haven't I haven't really focused on the border security piece here. I mean, it's fundamental Haven't said that today, but it is fundamental if you can't control who's coming in out of the country You can't have a rational discussion as a matter of public policy about who you think should be coming in and out of the country kind of to your",
