  {
    "episode_id": 92921,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92921.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Senator Dole used to describe it this way. He said what we always have to keep in mind is that the federal budget process, the appropriations process, the spending process, the process by which we decide how much money is going to be collected from taxpayers and spent on public purposes. It's a two-step process. The first step as a Republican is how little money can you get a consensus or coalition to agree to put on the table, because that's important for the long-term financial health of this country, the things we're just talking about in terms of deficits and spending. We've done a terrible job at that, maybe throughout our modern history, but certainly over the last several years. The second is once that decision is made, hopefully in a positive way, that you're getting those top line numbers moving in the right direction or at least slowing down the rate in which they're moving in the wrong direction. Then the question is, once the money is on the table, how much of it do you get directed to the priorities of the people that you represent or the priorities that you believe the country needs? And I think that's a useful framework. And sometimes we collapse both of them, which I think is what's happening here in this year-end process, as it always seems to be at the years-end, because people who lost out in the first round, they didn't get as much money on the table as they would prefer, think they have leverage at the end of the year to come force in notwithstanding those big picture decisions, what they want, and then you wind up with everything out of balance. I don't claim to know Mr. Musk. Well, I've mentioned his name twice, which is just because he's been in the news a lot talking about stuff. But we had a briefing the other day where he and Mr. Ramaswamy came and talked to the Republican conference, including those of us who are going to be new members, about what their project is, their doge project",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
