  {
    "episode_id": 92921,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92921.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 59,
    "turn_text": "And I have to admit, I was impressed by both of them that came across very, very thoughtfully in the room. But Musk said something that stuck with me, and I've shared it several times since I came back from that. He said, I've been very fortunate or very blessed in my life. I thought it was weren't his word, but that was his point. He said, I've lived the American dream. That wasn't his phrasing, but that was his point. He said, I've built some great companies. That is what he said. And then he said this, but none of that matters if the country fails, which is why I'm engaged in this now. And I think there's a lot of wisdom in that. I mean, sometimes we lose sight of the forest for the trees and the forest is we are on a path that is unsustainable in terms of the economics of this country. And we've got to at least slow down the rate of driving in the wrong direction.",
