    "turn_text": "We certainly shouldn't be using food as a weapon. I believe that very strongly. And I think that we do have to be very strongly advocating to open foreign markets for American exports, including, but not limited to our agricultural exports. We make a lot of aircraft here in Kansas as well, which we like to sell around the world. So we have a keen interest in expanding access to foreign markets. We just have to be careful that as we go about doing that, we don't unilaterally disarm other parts of our economy. It's a balance, it always has been, it always will be.",
