    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm grateful for the opportunity to serve. As I say, this was not something I anticipated this year, but sometimes opportunity presents itself, and you think you can make a difference, and so you seek it. And in this case, that happened, and the voters were kind enough to let me take a shot. And so, for the next two years, and I hope beyond, but certainly the next two years, I hope to be an effective voice for the people in the second congressional district, this country has serious problems, and we need people who are serious-minded to try to make progress on them. We're not going to fix all of this in short order. It took generations to get here, and it's more than just a political or legal problem. It's also, to some extent, a public acceptance problem. We don't have agreement in this country on some of our priorities, and so as a consequence, we've tried to be all things to all people, and unfortunately, there's not enough money to go around on that. For me, that's what the America First Agenda is about. I know people have different ideas of that and I respect that. But my view of America First is just you figure out what you can do today and tomorrow to put this country on a path that will make it better the day after that and the day after that and the day after that and to solve some of these problems. And I'm going to do my darn just each and every day to try to get some of that done.",
